  t["Existe algún alumno que no ha aprobado"] = "There is some student who has not passed";
  t["Existe inversa ⟺ el determinante no es cero."] = "An inverse exists ⟺ the determinant is not zero.";
  t["Existe solo si los dos límites laterales coinciden."] = "It exists only if the two one-sided limits agree.";
  t["Existe un número real sin raíz cuadrada real"] = "There is a real number with no real square root";
  t["Existe un triángulo con dos ángulos rectos"] = "There is a triangle with two right angles";
  t["Existe un triángulo sin dos ángulos rectos"] = "There is a triangle without two right angles";
  t["Existe una función continua que no es derivable"] = "There is a continuous function that is not differentiable";
  t["Existe, sin embargo, una manera de eliminar <strong>todas</strong> las variables de confusión de un plumazo, incluidas las que no se te han ocurrido y las que no sabes medir. Es una de las ideas más bonitas de la ciencia y consiste en algo aparentemente frívolo: decidir a suertes quién recibe el tratamiento."] = "There is, however, a way of eliminating <strong>all</strong> the confounding variables at a stroke, including those you have not thought of and those you do not know how to measure. It is one of the loveliest ideas in science and it consists of something apparently frivolous: deciding by lot who receives the treatment.";
  t["Existencia (Bolzano) y unicidad (monotonía) son dos argumentos distintos y el examen pide los dos. Bolzano por sí solo nunca da «exactamente una»."] = "Existence (Bolzano) and uniqueness (monotonicity) are two different arguments and the exam asks for both. Bolzano on its own never gives “exactly one”.";
