  t["Inclina el plano de corte y mira qué curva aparece. La familia entera depende de un solo ángulo."] = "Tilt the cutting plane and see which curve appears. The whole family depends on a single angle.";
  t["Inclusión-exclusión"] = "Inclusion-exclusion";
  t["Incompatible"] = "Inconsistent";
  t["Incompatible (3)"] = "Inconsistent (3)";
  t["Incompatible sería $0 = b$ con $b \\ne 0$. Aquí $0 = 0$ no contradice nada: solo sobra una ecuación."] = "Inconsistent would be $0 = b$ with $b \\ne 0$. Here $0 = 0$ contradicts nothing: one equation is simply redundant.";
  t["Incompatibles e independientes son casi lo contrario: si ocurre $A$, $B$ ya no puede ocurrir, así que saber que ha pasado $A$ cambia por completo la probabilidad de $B$."] = "Mutually exclusive and independent are almost opposites: if $A$ happens, $B$ can no longer happen, so knowing that $A$ has happened changes the probability of $B$ completely.";
  t["Incompatibles significa que no pueden ocurrir a la vez."] = "Mutually exclusive means they cannot happen at once.";
  t["Incompatibles, luego independientes"] = "Mutually exclusive, so independent";
  t["Incompatibles: $P(A \\cap B) = 0$. Independientes: $P(A \\cap B) = P(A)\\,P(B)$"] = "Mutually exclusive: $P(A \\cap B) = 0$. Independent: $P(A \\cap B) = P(A)\\,P(B)$";
  t["Incompatibles: no pueden darse a la vez, así que uno informa totalmente del otro. Independientes: uno no informa nada del otro. Casi opuestos."] = "Mutually exclusive: they cannot happen at once, so one tells you everything about the other. Independent: one tells you nothing about the other. Almost opposites.";
  t["Incompletas: atajo. Y en $ax^2+bx=0$ nunca dividas entre $x$ — perderías $x=0$."] = "Incomplete ones: use the shortcut. And in $ax^2+bx=0$ never divide by $x$ — you would lose $x=0$.";
  t["Incógnitas: $x$ = adultos, $y$ = niños."] = "Unknowns: $x$ = adults, $y$ = children.";
  t["Incógnitas: $x$ bolígrafos, $y$ cuadernos, $z$ gomas."] = "Unknowns: $x$ pens, $y$ notebooks, $z$ erasers.";
