  t["Resolver es aislar la incógnita haciendo <strong>lo mismo en los dos lados</strong>."] = "Solving is isolating the unknown by doing <strong>the same thing to both sides</strong>.";
  t["Resolver pesando"] = "Solving by weighing";
  t["Resolver por Cramer"] = "Solving by Cramer";
  t["Resolver triángulos es cómo se mide lo que no se puede alcanzar. Un topógrafo calcula la altura de una montaña midiendo un ángulo desde dos puntos conocidos; así se levantaron todos los mapas antes de los satélites, encadenando triángulos por un país entero, y así se midió por primera vez el Everest en 1852, con un error de pocos metros y sin pisarlo. Un carpintero que corta una escalera, un instalador que decide la inclinación de unas placas solares y una grúa que calcula su alcance hacen la misma cuenta."] = "Solving triangles is how you measure what cannot be reached. A surveyor works out the height of a mountain by measuring an angle from two known points; that is how every map was made before satellites, chaining triangles across a whole country, and that is how Everest was first measured in 1852, to within a few metres and without setting foot on it. A carpenter cutting a staircase, a fitter deciding the tilt of some solar panels and a crane working out its reach all make the same calculation.";
