  t["Tenemos tres incógnitas y vamos a imponer tres condiciones. La primera es que $P$ y $f$ valgan lo mismo en $0$. Sustituyendo $x=0$ en $P$ desaparece todo menos el primer término:"] = "We have three unknowns and we are going to impose three conditions. The first is that $P$ and $f$ be equal at $0$. Substituting $x=0$ into $P$ makes everything vanish but the first term:";
  t["Tener ecuación no basta. Para $x = 4$ salen dos valores, $y = 2$ e $y = -2$: dos salidas para una entrada."] = "Having an equation is not enough. For $x = 4$ two values come out, $y = 2$ and $y = -2$: two outputs for one input.";
  t["Tener infinitas cifras no basta para ser irracional. Lo que importa es si hay periodo, y aquí lo hay."] = "Having infinitely many digits is not enough to be irrational. What matters is whether there is a recurring period, and here there is one.";
